# This .gitignore file should be placed at the root of your Unity project directory
#
# Get latest from https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Unity.gitignore
#
.utmp/
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
*.log

# By default unity supports Blender asset imports, *.blend1 blender files do not need to be committed to version control.
*.blend1
*.blend1.meta

# MemoryCaptures can get excessive in size.
# They also could contain extremely sensitive data
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/

# Recordings can get excessive in size
/[Rr]ecordings/

# Uncomment this line if you wish to ignore the asset store tools plugin
# /[Aa]ssets/AssetStoreTools*

# Autogenerated Jetbrains Rider plugin
/[Aa]ssets/Plugins/Editor/JetBrains*
# Jetbrains Rider personal-layer settings
*.DotSettings.user

# Visual Studio cache directory
.vs/

# Gradle cache directory
.gradle/

# Autogenerated VS/MD/Consulo solution and project files
ExportedObj/
.consulo/
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.tmp
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# Unity3D generated meta files
*.pidb.meta
*.pdb.meta
*.mdb.meta

# Unity3D generated file on crash reports
sysinfo.txt

# Mono auto generated files
mono_crash.*

# Builds
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.unitypackage.meta
*.app

# Crashlytics generated file
crashlytics-build.properties

# TestRunner generated files
InitTestScene*.unity*

# Addressables default ignores, before user customizations
/ServerData
/[Aa]ssets/StreamingAssets/aa*
/[Aa]ssets/AddressableAssetsData/link.xml*
/[Aa]ssets/Addressables_Temp*
# By default, Addressables content builds will generate addressables_content_state.bin
# files in platform-specific subfolders, for example:
# /Assets/AddressableAssetsData/OSX/addressables_content_state.bin
/[Aa]ssets/AddressableAssetsData/*/*.bin*

# Visual Scripting auto-generated files
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Flow/UnitOptions.db
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Flow/UnitOptions.db.meta
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Core/Property Providers
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Core/Property Providers.meta

# Auto-generated scenes by play mode tests
/[Aa]ssets/[Ii]nit[Tt]est[Ss]cene*.unity*

# MCP screenshot-verification output (debug artifacts, not source)
/[Aa]ssets/[Ss]creenshots/

# Python bytecode cache (Tools/motionkb extractor)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# API key / secrets — NEVER commit (key.env holds OPENAI_API_KEY for the VLM authoring step)
*.env
key.env

# MotionKB render frames are TRACKED (they were ignored until 2026-08-05). They started as a
# disposable intermediate of the offline VLM proposal step, but under the Phase-2 architecture they
# are a RUNTIME RETRIEVAL INPUT: the agent fetches them as open-ended visual evidence to arbitrate
# between candidates whose closed-vocabulary semantic labels do not separate them. Two consequences
# make ignoring them wrong: (1) they are part of the consumed contract, not an intermediate;
# (2) regenerating them needs a running Unity editor + the MCP bridge, which would make restoring
# the pure-Python agent side depend on booting the engine. They are binary, so *.png routes them
# through git-lfs (see .gitattributes); their .meta stay in plain git.

# The bulk Mixamo corpus is UNTRACKED. It is ~2400 skinless FBX (~1 GB) fetched from mixamo.com
# and fully reproducible from Dataset/tools/mixamo_batch.py plus the catalog.json and _state.json
# beside it, so nothing about it is authored here. Tracking it would route every file through
# git-lfs on a repository whose LFS objects already total 3.2 GB and therefore cannot be pushed
# (ADR 0005). A clip becomes repo content only when it enters the knowledge base: at that point
# `git mv` it into a tracked animation folder, so the FBX and its KB entry still land in one
# commit and the .meta -- and therefore the guid the KB records -- travels with it.
/[Aa]ssets/[Aa]nimations/Mixamo30/
# ...and the folder's own .meta, so `git status` stays usable as the drift detector
# (ADR 0005) instead of permanently showing one untracked file.
/[Aa]ssets/[Aa]nimations/Mixamo30.meta

# ...and the pose dumps sampled from that corpus, for the same reason and by the same rule.
# A dump is JSON at about 5.6 KB per sampled frame; 2446 clips come to roughly 1.4 GB, some
# 600 MB packed. Tracking them would preserve only half a reproduction chain that is already
# broken at its source, since the FBX they were sampled from are untracked too — and it would
# grow a repository that already cannot be pushed. The candidate records built FROM them ARE
# tracked: those are knowledge base content, about 6 KB each. When a corpus clip is promoted
# into agent/animation_knowledge_base/actions/, its dump is added in the same commit as its FBX
# (ADR 0014; the path is ADR 0017's).
/agent/animation_knowledge_base/raw/mx_*.json

# ...and the render frames of those same corpus clips, by the same rule again. The eight nursing
# actions' frame directories above stay TRACKED: they are the consumed contract for eight records
# that ARE repo content. The corpus's are 2446 x 24 JPEG, about 3.4 GB, regenerable offline from the
# dumps with `ingest_corpus.py render` — and the reason the nursing frames had to be tracked (that
# regenerating them needs a live Unity editor, which the pure-Python agent side must not depend on)
# does not save these: the clips they show are untracked, so the engine could not regenerate them
# from a fresh clone anyway. A corpus clip that is promoted into the knowledge base brings its
# frames into the same commit as its FBX and its dump.
/agent/animation_knowledge_base/frames/mx_*/
